    <h1>Assignment 2: MLP Implementation & Visualization</h1>
    
    <h2>1. Task Description</h2>
    <p>Implement a 2-2-1 structure MLP network from scratch using TensorFlow to solve the XOR classification problem.</p >

    <h2>2. Core Implementation</h2>
    <p>Below is the key code for model definition and the training loop using GradientTape:</p >
    
    <!-- Python 代码块 -->
    <div class="code-block">
<pre><code>import tensorflow as tf
import numpy as np

# 1. Data Preparation
x = tf.constant([[0, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1]], dtype=tf.float64)
target = tf.constant([[0], [1], [1], [0]], dtype=tf.float64)

# 2. Initialize Parameters (Randomly)
W = tf.Variable(tf.random.normal([2, 2], dtype=tf.float64))
b_hidden = tf.Variable(tf.zeros([2], dtype=tf.float64))
v = tf.Variable(tf.random.normal([2, 1], dtype=tf.float64))
b_output = tf.Variable(tf.zeros([1], dtype=tf.float64))
parameters = [W, b_hidden, v, b_output]

# 3. Training Loop
optimizer = tf.keras.optimizers.SGD(learning_rate=0.5)

for epoch in range(1, 301):
    with tf.GradientTape() as tape:
        # Forward Propagation
        hidden = tf.sigmoid(tf.matmul(x, W) + b_hidden)
        logits = tf.matmul(hidden, v) + b_output
        
        # Calculate Loss
        loss = tf.reduce_mean(tf.nn.sigmoid_cross_entropy_with_logits(labels=target, logits=logits))
    
    # Backward Propagation
    gradients = tape.gradient(loss, parameters)
    optimizer.apply_gradients(zip(gradients, parameters))

print("Training finished.")</code></pre>
